# Pulse deployment context

```yaml
deployment:
  cloudProvider: aws

  environments:
    - name: local
      purpose: Docker Compose development and end-to-end surge demonstrations
      runCommand: docker compose up --build
      deployMechanism: Docker Compose
    - name: demo-aws
      purpose: Low-cost portfolio deployment using a small EC2 Auto Scaling Group and CloudWatch custom metrics
      runCommand: terraform -chdir=infra apply
      deployMechanism: Terraform plus EC2 launch template user data

  strategy:
    type: rolling
    featureFlags:
      - PULSE_DRY_RUN defaults to true
      - Live AWS scaling requires explicit configuration and credentials

  rollback:
    code: Revert the feature commit or pull request and rebuild the previous container image
    database: Run the corresponding Alembic downgrade; the initial and subsequent migrations must remain reversible
    config: Restore the previous environment values and re-run Docker Compose or Terraform plan/apply

  ci:
    provider: none-yet
    prChecks: The complete delivery must add GitHub Actions for lint, tests, migration compilation, dashboard build, and Terraform validation
    watchCommand: gh pr checks {number} --repo Suryavarma333/pulse-engine

  observability:
    apm: CloudWatch custom metrics and application metrics exposed by Pulse
    logs: Structured application logs plus PostgreSQL audit records for predictions, scaling actions, and shedding transitions
```
